  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Roads between mountain villages carry wild beasts, cliffs, hard weather, and dangerous wild Gu worms.",
      "chapters": [
        110
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Chainsaw Golden Centipede, a rank three wild Gu worm, shows the type in the field: wild Gu worms are crafty, and if that centipede senses something amiss it burrows and escapes.",
      "chapters": [
        129
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_chainsaw_golden_centipede"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A thousand beast king usually has three or four rank two and a rank three wild Gu worm residing on it.",
      "chapters": [
        150
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Wild Gu can use natural essence straight from the air, while Gu Masters can only use primeval essence from their own apertures.",
      "chapters": [
        164
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "natural-essence",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After a Gu Master dies, the Gu worms left behind still hold that person’s will. They cannot be considered wild Gu worms, and they have lost the ability to use natural essence in the air.",
      "chapters": [
        165
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "natural-essence",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Wild Gu worms possess their own will and can absorb natural primeval essence in the air by themselves. Once a Gu worm is refined by a Gu Master, its willpower is dominated by that Gu Master, and it loses the ability to absorb surrounding primeval essence. It can only absorb primeval essence from the Gu Master’s aperture.",
      "chapters": [
        183
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "after-refinement",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Gu after refinement as tools are covered on Gu worms.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "after-refinement",
